// A recipe, written from md-docs/recipes/open-a-socket.md by scripts/docsite/recipes.py;
// edit the recipe, not this file.
page RecipeOpenASocket(path: "/recipes/open-a-socket", title: "Open a socket — Recipes", description: "Hold a two-way connection to a server with a `socket`: it reconnects, keeps itself alive, and queues what you send while the line is down.") {
    RecipeShell("Open a socket", summary: "A `socket` holds a two-way connection to a server: chat, live editing, notifications. You declare it with `ws(…)` and read it with `match`, the way you read a `resource`. This chat page shows a spinner while the socket connects, the messages once it is open, and why it stopped when it closes:", outputs: ["website", "app", "desktop"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works"), Anchor(id: "choose-a-kind-of-connection", label: "Choose a kind of connection"), Anchor(id: "read-a-connection-s-state-and-messages", label: "Read a connection's state and messages"), Anchor(id: "troubleshooting", label: "Troubleshooting"), Anchor(id: "variations", label: "Variations")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Listen to server-sent events", to: "/recipes/server-sent-events"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Talk to the site's other tabs", to: "/recipes/talk-between-tabs"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Connect two readers' pages", to: "/recipes/connect-two-readers")], source: "md-docs/recipes/open-a-socket.md", how: true, hasVariations: true) {
        code {
            Markdown("**Needs:** a WebSocket server; change `wss://example.com/chat` to yours.")
            CodeBlock(#"page Chat(path: "/chat", title: "Chat", description: "Talk to the team.") {
    state draft = ""
    socket chat = ws("wss://example.com/chat", heartbeat: 20.seconds) {
        on message(m) { log(m) }
    }

    Heading("Chat").h1
    match chat {
        connecting { Spinner.sm }
        open       { for m in chat.messages by m.id { Text(m.text) } }
        closed(c)  { Alert("Disconnected ({c.code})").warning }
        error(e)   { Alert(e.message).danger }
    }
    Input(bind: draft, label: "Message").text
    Button("Send").primary { on click { chat.send({ text: draft })  draft = "" } }
}"#, title: "wf")
        }
        variations {
            Heading("Type the messages", id: "type-the-messages").h3

            Markdown("To have the compiler check what you send and type what you receive, name a type for each direction inside the socket's block with `send` and `receive`:")

            CodeBlock(#"type Incoming { id: String, text: String }
type Outgoing { text: String }

page Room(path: "/room", title: "Room", description: "A typed conversation.") {
    state draft = ""
    socket chat = ws("wss://example.com/chat", heartbeat: 20.seconds) {
        send    Outgoing
        receive Incoming
    }
    Heading("Room").h1
    for m in chat.messages by m.id { Text(m.text) }
    Input(bind: draft, label: "Message")
    Button("Send") { on click { chat.send(Outgoing(text: draft))  draft = "" } }
}"#, title: "wf")

            Markdown("With `send` and `receive` declared, `chat.send(…)` is checked against `Outgoing`, and each message in `chat.messages` is an `Incoming`, so `m.text` is a `String` and `m.txet` is an error.")

        }
        Markdown("A connection is read the same way a resource is, so this recipe assumes you know how a `resource` is read with `match` and its arms ([Fetching data](/learn/15-data#show-a-request-with-resource)), and how `state` and `effect` work ([State and reactivity](/learn/07-state-and-reactivity)).\n\n- **`socket chat = ws(…)`** opens the socket when the page is drawn and closes it when the reader leaves.\n- **`on message(m) \{ \}`**, inside the socket's block, handles each message that arrives. `on open \{ \}` runs each time the line opens — the first time and after every reconnection.\n- **`match chat`** takes the arms `connecting`, `open`, `closed(c)` and `error(e)`, and an `else` for the rest. `closed(c)` is handed the close, with `c.code` and `c.reason`; `error(e)` is handed the failure, with `e.message`.\n- **`chat.messages`** holds what arrived, in order, and **`chat.send(…)`** sends a value.\n\nA socket looks after itself:\n\n- **It reconnects.** When the line drops, it waits and tries again, doubling the wait each time up to a limit. A server that closes the line normally (code `1000`) is not reconnected to.\n- **It keeps itself alive.** With `heartbeat:`, it sends a ping that often and treats a missing answer as a dead line, which it closes and reopens.\n- **It holds what you send while it is down.** `chat.send(…)` while the socket is reconnecting queues the message and sends it when the line opens again.\n- **It reads JSON.** A text message that parses as JSON arrives as a value; any other text arrives as a string. A value you send is sent as JSON, unless it is already a string.")

        Heading("Tune a socket", id: "tune-a-socket").h3

        Markdown("Pass options after the address to change how a socket connects and reconnects:")

        Table(caption: "Tune a socket") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Option").header
                    Table.Cell("Does").header
                    Table.Cell("Default").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`protocols:`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("The subprotocols to ask for: `[\"v2\"]`") }
                    Table.Cell("none")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`heartbeat:`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Sends a ping this often, and reconnects when no pong comes back: `20.seconds`") }
                    Table.Cell("off")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`ping:`, `pong:`") }
                    Table.Cell("The heartbeat's messages")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`\"ping\"`, `\"pong\"`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`reconnect:`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`false` to stay closed after the server closes the line") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`true`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`delay:`, `max:`") }
                    Table.Cell("The first wait before reconnecting, in milliseconds, and the longest; the wait doubles each time")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`500`, `30000`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`queue:`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`false` to drop, rather than hold, what is sent while the socket is down") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`true`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`binaryType:`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`\"blob\"` or `\"arraybuffer\"`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`\"blob\"`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`keep:`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("How many messages `.messages` holds, the newest; the oldest go first") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`500`") }
                }
            }
        }

        Heading("Choose a kind of connection", id: "choose-a-kind-of-connection").h2

        Markdown("A socket is one of five kinds of connection. Pick the one that fits the job:")

        Table(caption: "Choose a kind of connection") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Declaration").header
                    Table.Cell("Opened with").header
                    Table.Cell("Use it for").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`socket`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`ws(url, …)`") }
                    Table.Cell("Two-way messages with a server: chat, live editing, notifications")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`stream`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`sse(url, …)`") }
                    Table.Cell("One-way messages from a server: prices, progress, a log")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`channel`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`broadcast(name)`") }
                    Table.Cell("Messages between tabs of your site in one browser")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`peer`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`rtc(signal:, …)`") }
                    Table.Cell("A direct line to another reader's page, with no server in the middle")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`worker`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`spawn(url, …)`") }
                    Table.Cell("A script of your site running beside the page, off its thread")
                }
            }
        }

        Heading("Read a connection's state and messages", id: "read-a-connection-s-state-and-messages").h2

        Markdown("Every connection is a *handle*: a value whose members follow the connection. A `match` reads its state, and text, an `if` or an `effect` reads what arrived:")

        Table(caption: "Read a connection's state and messages") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("").header
                    Table.Cell.header { Markdown("`socket`") }
                    Table.Cell.header { Markdown("`stream`") }
                    Table.Cell.header { Markdown("`channel`") }
                    Table.Cell.header { Markdown("`peer`") }
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.state`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`connecting`, `open`, `closed`, `error` — the arms of a `match`") }
                    Table.Cell("the same")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`open` or `closed`") }
                    Table.Cell("the same as a socket")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.messages`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("the messages, in order: the last 500, or `keep:`") }
                    Table.Cell("the same")
                    Table.Cell("—")
                    Table.Cell("the same")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.last(kind)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("the last message, or the last whose `type` is `kind`, among those `.messages` holds") }
                    Table.Cell("the last under an event's name")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.last`: the last posted") }
                    Table.Cell("as a socket")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.error`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("the failure, which the `error(e)` arm is handed") }
                    Table.Cell("the same")
                    Table.Cell("—")
                    Table.Cell("the same")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.closure`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("the close, which `closed(c)` is handed: `.code`, `.reason`") }
                    Table.Cell("—")
                    Table.Cell("—")
                    Table.Cell("the same")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Sending")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.send(value)` — queued while the line is down") }
                    Table.Cell("—")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.post(value)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.send(value)` — queued until it opens") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.close()`") }
                    Table.Cell("closes it early")
                    Table.Cell("the same")
                    Table.Cell("the same")
                    Table.Cell("the same")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.signal(m)`") }
                    Table.Cell("—")
                    Table.Cell("—")
                    Table.Cell("—")
                    Table.Cell("hands it what the other side signalled")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("A connection left open all day would otherwise hold every message it was ever sent, so `.messages` keeps the newest 500 and lets the oldest go. `keep:` on the connection says another number — `ws(url, keep: 50)`, `sse(url, keep: 2000)` — and `keep: 0` keeps none, for a connection whose `on message` handler stores what it needs itself.\n\nA store may hold any of these too. It opens the connection when the store is first read and closes it with the store; a page reads it as `Lang.css.state`, and the store's actions read it by its name.")

        Heading("Troubleshooting", id: "troubleshooting").h2

        Markdown("- **The socket never leaves `connecting`.** The server is not answering at that address. Check the scheme: a page served over HTTPS must use `wss://`, not `ws://`.\n- **The socket closes and does not come back.** The server closed it with code `1000`, or you set `reconnect: false`. A normal close is final; any other close reconnects.\n- **The socket reconnects every few seconds.** With `heartbeat:` set, the server must answer each `ping:` with the `pong:` text. A server that does not answer looks dead, and the socket reopens.\n- **`stream.last(\"name\")` is always null.** The event name is not in `events:`. Only the names listed there are listened to.\n- **The other tab does not hear a `channel` post.** A tab does not hear its own posts, and both tabs must be on the same origin and use the same channel name.\n- **Two peers on different networks never open.** Give `ice:` a STUN server. With none, only readers on the same network can connect.\n- **A worker request fails after 10 seconds.** The worker did not post back an answer with the request's `id`. Raise `timeout:` for slow work, or check the script answers every method it is sent.")

    }
}
